<urn:usf:acceptance:provider-cli-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "One confined offline suite proves the actual probe qualify handler selects both API-adapter and claude-cli routes through the same graph-derived economics, task-class suite, corpus, threshold policy and qualification evaluator. The CLI branch invokes one exact declared requested model per case through the existing bounded transport seam, seals only returned text into durable invocation observations, and preserves returned model, invocation identity and usage exactly as observed or null. A model-specific task-class qualification requires a non-null returned model exactly equal to the selected requested model. A stored null returned-model observation remains truthful but is unqualified and grants no task class; route selection, login, exit status and returned text cannot substitute for it. Absent or insecure session, absent executable, absent selected model, null or mismatched returned model, unsupported transport or option, refused invocation, timeout, missing text, partial observation set under the current all-dimension threshold, stale suite or policy, and unauthorised economic route grant no task class. Tests use a private in-process dependency seam with production defaults and make zero real provider calls." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
