<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Qualification grants no economic authorization. A qualified route that the operator has not authorised economically remains ineligible to execute, and the reverse holds: an authorised route holds no task class until it earns one." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The availability preflight and its economics contract are a separate concern and are not reached from this path. This contract removes qualification's dependency on them; it does not change what they mean or claim to replace them." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The pure semantic evaluator remains externalContact false because it evaluates supplied authenticated observations only. The qualification runner that creates those observations is a distinct externalContact true operation." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The route-result schema is in this write set because it pins the qualification reference shape with additionalProperties false, so the record and the schema that describes it cannot move independently. The route-qualification-receipt and parallel-provider-run schemas are deliberately excluded: their model-identity definitions describe the invocation and probe surfaces rather than a qualification, and their validations pass unchanged." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Two further validations are in this write set because they assert the shape this contract changes. provider-cli.test.ts supplies probe semantic an input fixture in the retired shape, and graph-lanes.test.ts asserts a policy-covered lane count that any new lane moves. Neither is provider archaeology; both are direct consequences of the boundary change." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Extend the shared provider task-class qualification runner to admitted subscription CLI routes while retaining one suite, grader, threshold policy, result identity, durable observation model and economic authorization boundary across API and CLI transports." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
<urn:usf:contract:provider-cli-qualification:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Measured on 2026-09-04 at semantic digest 113271c04753. Qualification took a ProviderProbeResult plus an answers array. The probe proved only that the route replied to one fixed probe prompt, and the answers were unauthenticated caller input: nothing in assertProbeBinding or qualifySemanticProfile tied any answer to any invocation, so a caller could supply sixteen answers the model never produced and the suite would grade them. The same binding also required probe.quota available, probe.health available and probe.cost observed at zero -- commercial-account facts that the qualification requirement itself does not ask for, and that only an authenticated provider-console observation could establish, which is why no route had ever qualified." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
