<urn:usf:requirement:cli-observation-preserves-known-and-unknown> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Each accepted CLI answer binds provider, requested model, transport, case, prompt digest, answer digest, execution-evidence digest and observed time. The observation and semantic-result schemas preserve returned model, invocation identity and input/output/total usage exactly when exposed and retain null when the transport does not expose them; null carries no authenticity or usage claim. A null actual returned model may be stored as an honest observation but must yield an unqualified result with no derived task-class role. A non-null returned model inconsistent with the requested route refuses the whole set; only a non-null exact match may participate in qualification." <urn:usf:graph:provider-cli-qualification> .
